.TH RAMDISK 7 "31 October 2026" "ramdisk"
.SH NAME
ramdisk \- the RAM disk: the boot loader's miniroot and two scratch disks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/dsk/ram0
.br
.B /dev/dsk/ram1
.br
.B /dev/dsk/ram2
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ramdisk
is a block driver with three units, each a disk held in memory.
.TP
.B ram0
the miniroot image the boot loader placed in memory, when there is one.
A medium that boots from a RAM disk (a CD, a floppy, a network install)
carries the image, and the kernel mounts its root from this unit.
The memory is the loader's: the kernel never uses it for anything else,
and the driver never frees it.
The unit can be written to; its contents are lost at power-off.
Without an image the unit does not exist.
.TP
.B ram1
a scratch disk of
.B size1
KiB, 512 by default.
.TP
.B ram2
a scratch disk of
.B size2
KiB, 2048 by default.
.PP
A scratch disk's memory is taken when the unit is first opened (or
mounted) and given back when the last user closes it; a fresh scratch
disk reads as zeros.
It is taken in pieces of at most 256 KiB.
When the kernel cannot give it, the open fails with
.B ENOMEM
and can simply be tried again later.
A unit whose size is 0 does not exist.
.PP
Every transfer is a copy by the CPU.
There is no raw (character) device.
.PP
The driver is the loadable module
.BR ramdisk ,
of the root class: the boot loader places it with the kernel, and it is
linked before the root file system is mounted.
It replaces the stock
.B ram
driver on the same block major, with the stock sizes for units 1 and 2.
It is never unloaded.
.SH PARAMETERS
.TP
.BI size1= KiB
.PD 0
.TP
.BI size2= KiB
.PD
the sizes of the scratch disks, 0 to 16384.
A line
.B "param size2=4096"
in
.B /etc/conf/modreg.local.d/ramdisk
sets one;
.B kbootset build
takes it into the next boot generation.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
An open of a unit that does not exist gives
.BR ENXIO ,
an open of a scratch disk the kernel has no memory for
.BR ENOMEM .
A transfer past the end of a unit gives
.BR ENXIO ;
a read that starts exactly at the end reads nothing.
At load the console says where unit 0's image is
.RB ( "ramdisk: unit 0 is the image at" ...).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.ft CW
mkfs /dev/dsk/ram2 4096
mount /dev/dsk/ram2 /mnt
.ft R
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.BR /dev/dsk/ram0 ", " ram1 ", " ram2
block major 20, minors 0 to 2, mode 0600, owner root.
.TP
.B /etc/conf/mod.d/ramdisk
the module.
.TP
.B /etc/conf/modreg.local.d/ramdisk
the box's own parameters, which no package owns.
